- Spectral type luminosity class III (giants) or IIICN (giant with CN anomaly) strongly indicates giants.  
- Absolute magnitude (Amag) is brighter (lower) for giants, roughly below 15 in examples.  
- B-V color index tends to be higher (redder) for giants in examples given.  
- Parallax is higher for some giants but not a strict rule; combined with Amag and SpType it helps.  
- Vmag is less decisive alone but giants in examples tend to have Vmag < 8.  
